\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Integrated the static spherical Einstein equations and checked the Schwarzschild–AdS exterior horizon; no rigidity among nonspherical static metrics.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the full supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and listed references for 30006045. No fresh status or novelty search was performed. The argument below proves its auxiliary statements directly and does not import an unverified external theorem.

\paragraph{Solving the spherical ansatz.} Restrict to a four-dimensional static spherically symmetric exterior
\[
 g=-e^{2\Phi(r)}F(r)dt^2+F(r)^{-1}dr^2+r^2d\Omega^2,
 \qquad F>0,
\]
with \(\Lambda=-3/\ell^2\), \(\ell>0\). Direct computation of the mixed Einstein tensor gives \(G^t{}_t=(rF'+F-1)/r^2\) and \(G^r{}_r-G^t{}_t=2F\Phi'/r\). The vacuum equations \(G^a{}_b+\Lambda\delta^a_b=0\) therefore imply
\[
 (rF)'=1+3r^2/\ell^2,\qquad \Phi'=0.
\]
Integration gives \(F=1-2M/r+r^2/\ell^2\); a constant change of the time coordinate removes \(\Phi\). Substitution in the angular equation verifies it as well: with constant \(\Phi\), \(G^\theta{}_\theta=F'/r+F''/2=3/\ell^2\).
\paragraph{Boundary and horizon test.} For \(M>0\), \(F'=2M/r^2+2r/\ell^2>0\), while \(F\to-\infty\) at zero and \(F\to+\infty\) at infinity. There is exactly one positive simple zero, delimiting this static exterior. For \(M=0\), no such positive horizon occurs. The normalization of time still has to match the specified conformal boundary.
\paragraph{First uniqueness gap.} Spherical symmetry was assumed, whereas the source seeks uniqueness among the relevant static Einstein competitors. The calculation cannot derive spherical symmetry from a spherical conformal boundary and the appropriate horizon/regularity hypotheses; nor does it specify all global topologies. That rigidity step, with exact source boundary data, is the first gap. The familiar ansatz calculation is not a full static uniqueness theorem.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked the mixed Einstein components, angular equation, time normalization, positive-mass simple horizon and zero-mass boundary case. Model self-audit only; no independent human mathematical verification. Applied contribution prompt A before drafting and B afterwards. Checked the mixed Einstein components, angular equation, time normalization, positive-mass simple horizon and zero-mass boundary case. First remaining gap: Prove symmetry and global rigidity from the precise source conformal-boundary, horizon and regularity hypotheses. The inherited source status is preserved; original-target completion remains zero.

Coordinator checked the radial Einstein equations, integrated lapse and positive-mass simple horizon under spherical symmetry. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file tools used to read definitions and serialize manuscripts. Calculations are symbolic reasoning; no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

